@startuml
layout compact
package Headliner {
  component OPC <<BackendService>> {
    require "Publish" as opc_publish
  }
  component trips <<TopicExchange>> {
    provide "Publish" as trips_publish
  }
  component Notifications <<BackendService>> {
    portin "notifications.trips" as notifications_queue
    require "SMTP" as notifications_smtp
  }
  component Loyalty <<BackendService>> {
    portin "loyalty.trips" as loyalty_queue
  }
  component WarehouseETL <<BackendService>> {
    portin "warehouse.all" as warehouse_queue
  }
  component AffiliateRelay <<BackendService>> {
    portin "affiliates.trips" as affiliates_queue
    require "Webhook" as affiliates_webhook
  }
  component SupportConsole <<WebApplication>> {
    portin "support.cancellations" as support_queue
  }
  component ShuttlePlanner <<BackendService>> {
    portin "shuttle.planning" as shuttle_queue
  }
}
component MailRelay <<ExternalSystem>> {
  provide "SMTP" as mail_smtp
}
component AffiliatePartners <<ExternalSystem>> {
  provide "Webhook" as partners_webhook
}
trips_publish --> opc_publish
notifications_queue -- trips : <<subscribe>> {binding = "trip.confirmed, trip.cancelled, trip.failed"}
loyalty_queue -- trips : <<subscribe>> {binding = "trip.confirmed"}
warehouse_queue -- trips : <<subscribe>> {binding = "#"}
affiliates_queue -- trips : <<subscribe>> {binding = "trip.*"}
support_queue -- trips : <<subscribe>> {binding = "trip.cancelled"}
shuttle_queue -- trips : <<subscribe>> {binding = "supplier.shuttle.*"}
mail_smtp --> notifications_smtp
partners_webhook --> affiliates_webhook
note top of trips
trips is a topic exchange
(deploy/broker.toml:4) in the message
broker, which services reach over AMQP
(deploy/services.toml:16).
The OPC publishes trip.<status> and
supplier.<kind>.<status> events
(services/opc/events.py:12).
In a binding key, * matches exactly one
word and # matches zero or more words
(infra/broker.py:48).
Bindings:
deploy/broker.toml:16 loyalty.trips
deploy/broker.toml:21 warehouse.all
deploy/broker.toml:26 affiliates.trips
deploy/broker.toml:31 support.cancellations
deploy/broker.toml:36 shuttle.planning
services/notifications/consumers.py:25
notifications.trips
end note
note bottom of OPC
Key: UML 2.5.1 component diagram.
Stereotypes from the Headliner
architecture profile: «BackendService»,
«WebApplication», «TopicExchange»,
«ExternalSystem».
Ball and socket: a synchronous call;
the socket side calls and waits.
«subscribe» {binding}: the exchange
copies each event whose routing key
matches the binding into the
consumer's queue, named on its port.
end note
@enduml
